rmodynamic gains inside the pump housing, the oil temperature increases by $\\Delta T = 1.8\\text{ K}$ between the inlet and outlet.\n* Specific heat capacity of the oil ($c_p$) = $1900\\text{ J/(kg}\\cdot\\text{K)}$.\n\n\n3. **Mechanical Power & Efficiency (`mechanics`):**\n* Overall efficiency of the pump unit ($\\eta_{\\text{overall}}$) = $78\\% = 0.78$.\n\n\n\n---\n\n### **🎯 Required Calculations:**\n\n1. **Inlet and Outlet Fluid Velocities ($v_1, v_2$):**\n* Calculate the fluid velocity in the suction pipe ($v_1$) and discharge pipe ($v_2$) in $\\text{m/s}$.\n\n\n2. **Hydraulic Power ($P_{\\text{hydraulic}}$):**\n* Calculate the static hydraulic power output required to lift the fluid by head $H$ in $\\text{kW}$.\n\n\n3. **Thermal Energy Transfer Rate ($P_{\\text{thermal}}$):**\n* Calculate the rate of thermal energy gained by the fluid due to the temperature rise $\\Delta T$ in $\\text{kW}$.\n\n\n4. **Total Required Pump Shaft Power ($P_{\\text{shaft}}$):**\n* Calculate the total input shaft power required by the pump drive ($\\text{kW}$) by combining the hydraulic, kinetic, and thermal power components using the unified equation:\n\n\n\n$$P_{\\text{shaft}} = \\frac{\\rho \\cdot Q \\cdot \\left( g \\cdot H + \\frac{v_2^2 - v_1^2}{2} + c_p \\cdot \\Delta T \\right)}{\\eta_{\\text{overall}}}$$'}], 'model': 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 'n': 1, 'reasoning_effort': None, 'reasoning_format': None, 'service_tier': 'on_demand', 'stop': None, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.7, 'tools': [{'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_force', 'description': "Calculate force using Newton's second law.\n\nFormula:\n    F = m * a\n\nArgs:\n    mass: Mass in kilograms (kg).\n    acceleration: Acceleration in meters per second squared (m/s²).\n\nReturns:\n    Force in Newtons (N).", 'parameters': {'properties': {'mass': {'type': 'number'}, 'acceleration': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['mass', 'acceleration'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_mass', 'description': 'Calculate mass from force and acceleration.\n\nFormula:\n    m = F / a\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    acceleration: Acceleration in meters per second squared (m/s²).\n\nReturns:\n    Mass in kilograms (kg).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'acceleration': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'acceleration'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_acceleration', 'description': 'Calculate acceleration from force and mass.\n\nFormula:\n    a = F / m\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    mass: Mass in kilograms (kg).\n\nReturns:\n    Acceleration in meters per second squared (m/s²).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'mass': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'mass'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_torque', 'description': 'Calculate torque.\n\nFormula:\n    τ = r * F * sin(θ)\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    lever_arm: Distance from pivot in meters (m).\n    angle: Angle between force and lever arm in degrees.\n\nReturns:\n    Torque in Newton-meters (N·m).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'lever_arm': {'type': 'number'}, 'angle': {'default': 90.0, 'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'lever_arm'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_work', 'description': 'Calculate mechanical work.\n\nFormula:\n    W = F * d * cos(θ)\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    displacement: Displacement in meters (m).\n    angle: Angle between force and displacement in degrees.\n\nReturns:\n    Work in Joules (J).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'displacement': {'type': 'number'}, 'angle': {'default': 0.0, 'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'displacement'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_energy', 'description': 'Calculate kinetic energy.\n\nFormula:\n    KE = 1/2 * m * v²\n\nArgs:\n    mass: Mass in kilograms (kg).\n    velocity: Velocity in meters per second (m/s).\n\nReturns:\n    Kinetic energy in Joules (J).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'mass': {'type': 'number'}, 'velocity': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['mass', 'velocity'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_power', 'description': 'Calculate mechanical power.\n\nFormula:\n    P = W / t\n\nArgs:\n    work: Work in Joules (J).\n    time: Time in seconds (s).\n\nReturns:\n    Power in Watts (W).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'work': {'type': 'number'}, 'time': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['work', 'time'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_stress', 'description': 'Calculate normal stress.\n\nFormula:\n    σ = F / A\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    area: Cross-sectional area in square meters (m²).\n\nReturns:\n    Stress in Pascals (Pa).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'area': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'area'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_strain', 'description': 'Calculate normal strain.\n\nFormula:\n    ε = ΔL / L₀\n\nArgs:\n    change_in_length: Change in length in meters (m).\n    original_length: Original length in meters (m).\n\nReturns:\n    Strain (dimensionless).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'change_in_length': {'type': 'number'}, 'original_length': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['change_in_length', 'original_length'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'fluid_flow', 'description': 'Calculate basic fluid-flow parameters for flow through a circular pipe.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\nREYNOLDS NUMBER\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\n    Re = rho * V * D / mu\n\nwhere:\n    rho = fluid density [kg/m^3]\n    V   = average fluid velocity [m/s]\n    D   = pipe diameter [m]\n    mu  = dynamic viscosity [Pa.s]\n\nFlow regime:\n    Re < 2300       -> approximately laminar\n    2300-4000       -> transitional\n    Re > 4000       -> turbulent\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\nFLOW RATE\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\n    Q = V * A\n\nFor a circular pipe:\n\n    A = pi * D^2 / 4\n\nTherefore:\n\n    Q = V * pi * D^2 / 4\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\nVELOCITY\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\n    V = Q / A\n\nTherefore:\n\n    V = 4Q / (pi * D^2)\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\nPRESSURE LOSS\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nDarcy-Weisbach equation:\n\n    Delta_P = f * (L/D) * (rho*V^2/2)\n\nwhere:\n    f = Darcy friction factor\n    L = pipe length [m]\n    D = pipe diameter [m]\n\nFriction factor:\n\nLaminar:\n    f = 64/Re\n\nTurbulent:\n    Swamee-Jain approximation:\n\n    f = 0.25 /\n        [log10(e/(3.7D) + 5.74/Re^0.9)]^2\n\nwhere:\n    e = absolute pipe roughness [m]\n\nThe tool automatically determines the flow regime from Re.\n\nUnits:\n    density        -> kg/m^3\n    viscosity      -> Pa.s\n    diameter       -> m\n    length         -> m\n    velocity       -> m/s\n    flow rate      -> m^3/s\n    pressure loss  -> Pa\n    roughness      -> m\n\nAssumptions:\n    - Circular pipe\n    - Steady flow\n    - Newtonian fluid\n    - Constant properties\n    - Fully developed internal flow\n    - Darcy-Weisbach pressure loss\n    - Minor losses from valves/fittings are not included', 'parameters': {'properties': {'operation': {'enum': ['reynolds_number', 'pressure_loss', 'flow_rate', 'velocity'], 'type': 'string'}, 'density': {'type': 'number'}, 'viscosity': {'type': 'number'}, 'pipe_diameter': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'pipe_length': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'velocity_value': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'flow_rate_value': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'pressure_loss_value': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'roughness': {'default': 0.0, 'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['operation', 'density', 'viscosity'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'pump_power', 'description': 'Calculate pump hydraulic power, shaft power, and pump head.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n1. HYDRAULIC POWER\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nHydraulic power:\n\n    P_h = Q * DeltaP\n\nwhere:\n\n    P_h = hydraulic power [W]\n    Q   = volumetric flow rate [m^3/s]\n    DeltaP = pressure increase [Pa]\n\nHydraulic power can also be calculated from head:\n\n    P_h = rho * g * Q * H\n\nwhere:\n\n    rho = fluid density [kg/m^3]\n    g   = gravitational acceleration [m/s^2]\n    H   = pump head [m]\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n2. SHAFT POWER\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nShaft power is the hydraulic power divided by pump efficiency:\n\n    P_shaft = P_h / eta\n\nTherefore:\n\n    P_shaft = Q * DeltaP / eta\n\nor:\n\n    P_shaft = rho * g * Q * H / eta\n\nwhere:\n\n    eta = pump efficiency\n\nEfficiency must be between 0 and 1.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n3. PUMP HEAD\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nPump head from pressure difference:\n\n    H = DeltaP / (rho * g)\n\nwhere:\n\n    H = pump head [m]\n    DeltaP = pressure difference [Pa]\n    rho = fluid density [kg/m^3]\n    g = gravitational acceleration [m/s^2]\n\nUnits:\n\n    flow_rate        -> m^3/s\n    pressure_difference -> Pa\n    density          -> kg/m^3\n    head             -> m\n    efficiency       -> 0 to 1\n    hydraulic power  -> W\n    shaft power      -> W\n\nAssumptions:\n\n    - Steady-state operation\n    - Constant fluid density\n    - Pump efficiency is known\n    - Pressure_difference represents the pressure\n      increase produced by the pump', 'parameters': {'properties': {'operation': {'enum': ['hydraulic_power', 'shaft_power', 'pump_head'], 'type': 'string'}, 'flow_rate': {'type': 'number'}, 'pressure_difference': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'head': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'density': {'default': 1000.0, 'type': 'number'}, 'efficiency': {'default': 1.0, 'type': 'number'}, 'gravity': {'default': 9.81, 'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['operation', 'flow_rate'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'thermodynamics', 'description': 'Solve basic thermodynamic calculations.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\nSIGN CONVENTION\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nThe First Law is written as:\n\n    ΔU = Q - W\n\nwhere:\n\n    ΔU = change in internal energy [J]\n    Q  = heat added to the system [J]\n    W  = work done BY the system [J]\n\nTherefore:\n\n    Q = ΔU + W\n\n    W = Q - ΔU\n\nPositive Q:\n    Heat enters the system.\n\nPositive W:\n    System performs work on the surroundings.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n1. WORK\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nFor constant pressure boundary work:\n\n    W = P * ΔV\n\nwhere:\n\n    P  = pressure [Pa]\n    ΔV = volume change [m^3]\n\nPositive ΔV means expansion and positive work.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n2. HEAT\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nFirst Law:\n\n    Q = ΔU + W\n\nFor a substance heated without phase change:\n\n    Q = m * c * ΔT\n\nIf sufficient information is provided, the tool uses:\n\n    Q = m*c*ΔT\n\nOtherwise, when internal energy change and work\nare provided:\n\n    Q = ΔU + W\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n3. INTERNAL ENERGY\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nFirst Law:\n\n    ΔU = Q - W\n\nFor a simple sensible-heating process:\n\n    ΔU = m*c_v*ΔT\n\nHere `specific_heat` is treated as the appropriate\nspecific heat for the supplied problem.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n4. ENTHALPY\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\n    H = U + PV\n\nTherefore:\n\n    ΔH = ΔU + Δ(PV)\n\nFor constant pressure:\n\n    ΔH = ΔU + P*ΔV\n\nFor sensible heating using a specific heat:\n\n    ΔH = m*c_p*ΔT\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n5. EFFICIENCY\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\n    efficiency = useful output / input\n\nTherefore:\n\n    eta = E_out / E_in\n\nor, if efficiency is already known:\n\n    E_out = eta * E_in\n\nEfficiency is returned as a decimal between 0 and 1.\n\nUnits:\n\n    pressure       -> Pa\n    volume_change  -> m^3\n    heat/work      -> J\n    mass           -> kg\n    specific_heat  -> J/(kg*K)\n    temperature    -> K or deg C difference\n    enthalpy       -> J\n    internal energy -> J', 'parameters': {'properties': {'operation': {'enum': ['work', 'heat', 'internal_energy', 'enthalpy', 'efficiency'], 'type': 'string'}, 'heat': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'work': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'pressure': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'volume_change': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'mass': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'specific_heat': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'temperature_change': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'internal_energy_initial': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'internal_energy_final': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'enthalpy_initial': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'enthalpy_final': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'efficiency_value': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'energy_input': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'energy_output': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}}, 'required': ['operation'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'heat_transfer', 'description': "Calculate heat transfer by conduction, convection, and radiation.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n1. CONDUCTION\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nFourier's law for one-dimensional steady conduction\nthrough a flat wall:\n\n    Q_dot = k * A * ΔT / L\n\nwhere:\n\n    Q_dot = heat-transfer rate [W]\n    k     = thermal conductivity [W/(m*K)]\n    A     = area [m^2]\n    ΔT    = temperature difference [K]\n    L     = wall thickness [m]\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n2. CONVECTION\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nNewton's law of cooling:\n\n    Q_dot = h * A * (Ts - Tinf)\n\nwhere:\n\n    h    = convection coefficient [W/(m^2*K)]\n    A    = surface area [m^2]\n    Ts   = surface temperature [K or °C]\n    Tinf = fluid/bulk temperature [K or °C]\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n3. RADIATION\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nStefan-Boltzmann equation:\n\n    Q_dot = ε * σ * A * (Ts^4 - Tsur^4)\n\nwhere:\n\n    ε    = surface emissivity\n    σ    = Stefan-Boltzmann constant\n         = 5.670374419e-8 W/(m^2*K^4)\n    A    = radiating area [m^2]\n    Ts   = surface absolute temperature [K]\n    Tsur = surroundings absolute temperature [K]\n\nRadiation temperatures MUST be in Kelvin.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n4. HEAT RATE\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nIf heat_rate_value is supplied, the tool returns it.\n\nOtherwise, heat_rate calculates the heat-transfer rate\nusing the available heat-transfer information.\n\nSupported modes:\n\n    conduction\n    convection\n    radiation\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\nSIGN CONVENTION\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nPositive heat rate:\n    heat flows from the hotter region toward the colder\n    region.\n\nNegative heat rate:\n    the supplied temperature ordering causes heat flow in\n    the opposite direction.\n\nUnits:\n\n    heat rate -> W\n    area -> m^2\n    thickness -> m\n    temperature difference -> K\n    conductivity -> W/(m*K)\n    convection coefficient -> W/(m^2*K)\n    emissivity -> dimensionless", 'parameters': {'properties': {'operation': {'enum': ['conduction', 'convection', 'radiation', 'heat_rate'], 'type': 'string'}, 'thermal_conductivity': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'area': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'temperature_difference': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'thickness': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'convection_coefficient': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'surface_temperature': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'fluid_temperature': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'emissivity': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'surface_temperature_radiation': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'surroundings_temperature': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'heat_rate_value': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}}, 'required': ['operation'], 'type': 'object'}}}]}}
